{"title":"Associative property","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Associative_property&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p><p>A <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Binary_operation\" title=\"Binary operation\">binary operation</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/1/c11cf1795f9f312158d046b0e3a2bd6806837397.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G: S\\times S \\to S$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"116\" height=\"13\" /> is said to have the <b>associative property</b> or to <i>be associative</i> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/4/36422e52d87bb3e64f271fce6a5eaf750d342cdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G(a, G(b, c)) = G(G(a, b), c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"219\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/4/88479cba5eb99ebe10b309338f629abbdb657cb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c \\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" />.  Associativity is one of the most basic properties an operation can have.\n</p><p>For instance, the operation \"<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/c/77cf26be132ef93923e082ee4153b2cb0ef44a50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" />\" on the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real_number\" title=\"Real number\">real numbers</a> is associative because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/0/74089821630ec516c7a5a66020a9ad5cc26b5e5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + (b + c) = (a + b) + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"192\" height=\"18\" /> for all real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc6d9a6172d35127b6cb37ea92192caf7029a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>If we have an operation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/3/7f3b4ea3b8abe9ced6095c7d75f207a1127ee843.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"7\" /> which is written between its arguments (like \"<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/c/77cf26be132ef93923e082ee4153b2cb0ef44a50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" />\" or \"<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/c/bac4dbe1c696d11e8dc43dd7f613199b2120daa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\times$\" width=\"11\" height=\"9\" />\" <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematical_convention\" title=\"Mathematical convention\">conventionally</a> are), associativity tells us that we may write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70e0f9d4b9efee98652071488e3b5005863972b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\circ b \\circ c$\" width=\"60\" height=\"12\" /> unambiguously -- it does not matter which pair we combine first.\n</p><p><br />\nFor a non-example, consider the operation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/4/7b483825b688f22c482c60e0d7ce6010614d7a1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\circ: \\mathbb {R \\times R \\to R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"113\" height=\"12\" /> given by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/5/18504e89c63dd745189d9599fe339fada7ce78ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\circ b = a + 2b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"14\" />.  This operation is <i>not</i> associative because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/6/2c6a18cf1869179bf1e8ef8741c6e5b604e4d17d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\circ(b\\circ c) = a \\circ(b + 2c) = a + 2b + 4c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"298\" height=\"18\" /> while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/3/6131ce64b395505c93c86b437f44f60834f4dcaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a \\circ b)\\circ c = (a + 2b)\\circ c = a + 2b + 2c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"298\" height=\"18\" /> and those <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Expression\" title=\"Expression\">expressions</a> are not equal for all choices of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc6d9a6172d35127b6cb37ea92192caf7029a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> (in particular, they differ whenever <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/5/3a5061ac0ea7f3b0c9eb6387005ae6c28eac6bfe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />).\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018022435\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.022 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 55/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 301/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2950/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.356      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    6.356      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3830:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018022435 and revision id 9537. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}